  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "In the only movie theatre in Chefland, there is a single long row of MMM seats. The seats are indexed 111 to MMM from left to right. There is exactly one ticket for each individual seat. NNN people, numbered 111 to NNN, want to buy tickets for seats in this row.\n\nPerson iii wants exactly SiS_iSi​ number of tickets. They also have a strong preference for viewing angles. Specifically, person iii requires that each of their seats must be indexed between AiA_iAi​ and BiB_iBi​. It is guaranteed that Ai≥Ai−1A_i \\ge A_{i-1}Ai​≥Ai−1​ for 2≤i≤N2 \\le i \\le N2≤i≤N.\n\nFor each iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N), calculate the largest jjj (i≤j≤Ni ≤ j ≤ Ni≤j≤N) such that all people from iii to jjj can be accommodated together and given tickets according to their requirements.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains TTT - the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains two integers NNN and MMM - the number of people and seats respectively.\nNNN lines then follow. The iii-th line contains integers AiA_iAi​, BiB_iBi​, and SiS_iSi​ - the acceptable seat indices for person iii and the required number of tickets.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a single line with NNN space-separated integers. The iii-th of these integers should be the largest valid jjj (i≤j≤Ni \\leq j \\leq Ni≤j≤N) such that all people from iii to jjj can be accommodated together.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤5⋅1041 \\le T \\le 5 \\cdot 10^41≤T≤5⋅104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤M≤1091 \\le M \\le 10^91≤M≤109",
      "1≤Ai≤Bi≤M1 \\le A_i \\le B_i \\le M1≤Ai​≤Bi​≤M",
      "Ai≥Ai−1A_i \\ge A_{i-1}Ai​≥Ai−1​ for 2≤i≤N2 \\le i \\le N2≤i≤N",
      "1≤Si≤Bi−Ai+11 \\le S_i\\le B_i-A_i+11≤Si​≤Bi​−Ai​+1",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases is at most 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
