        "input": "2\n7 10\n2 10 5\n3 10 5\n4 9 1\n5 9 5\n6 8 1\n7 8 1\n8 8 1\n3 10\n2 10 9\n2 9 1\n8 9 1",
        "output": "1 3 4 4 7 7 7\n1 3 3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111:\n\ni=1i = 1i=1: It can be shown that person 222 cannot be accommodated with person 111. The maximum valid jjj in this case is 111 itself.\ni=2i = 2i=2: We can accommodate persons 222 and 333 together, and more people after person 333 cannot be accommodated. One way to do this is by ensuring that the set of seats assigned to person 222 is {3,4,6,7,8}\\{3, 4, 6, 7, 8 \\}{3,4,6,7,8} and to person 333 is {5}\\{5 \\}{5}.\ni=3i = 3i=3: We can accommodate persons 333 and 444 together, and more people after person 444 cannot be accommodated. One way to do this is by ensuring that the set of seats assigned to person 333 is {4}\\{4 \\}{4} and to person 444 is {5,6,7,8,9}\\{ 5, 6, 7, 8, 9 \\}{5,6,7,8,9}.\ni=4i = 4i=4: We cannot accommodate more people after person 444.\ni=5i = 5i=5: We can accommodate all persons 555, 666, and 777 together. One way to do this is by ensuring that the set of seats assigned to person 555 is {6}\\{6 \\}{6}, to person 666 is {7}\\{ 7 \\}{7}, and to person 777 is {8}\\{ 8 \\}{8}.\ni=6i = 6i=6: We can accommodate persons 666 and 777 together. One way to do this is by ensuring that the set of seats assigned to person 666 is {7}\\{ 7 \\}{7} and to person 777 is {8}\\{ 8 \\}{8}.\ni=7i = 7i=7: The maximum jjj possible is 777 itself."
